# srfi-42: repair indexed enumeration of multiple vectors (#513)
#
# :parallel supplies each inner generator's continuation. Passing cc again
# makes the indexed multi-vector branch bind a continuation form as a variable.
# Remove that extra argument, as in the indexed :list and :range rules.
# https://srfi.schemers.org/srfi-42/srfi-42.html
#
# Authorized correctness repair under the #429 patch workflow (2026-09-27).
# Both Patina backends, Chibi 0.12 and Gauche 0.9.15 reproduce the failure
# with the pinned implementation. With this correction all 28 SRFI 42 and
# 15 SRFI 78 smoke assertions pass on all four, including indexed vector
# concatenation, empty inputs and the dependent check-ec expansion.
# Reference staging removes only the inert #f library declaration rejected
# by Gauche; implementation bodies match the patched corpus. The pristine
# vendor extraction stays unchanged.
--- a/srfi/42.scm
+++ b/srfi/42.scm
@@ -438,7 +438,7 @@
           ((+ i 1))))
 
     ((_ cc var (index i) arg1 arg2 arg ...)
-     (:parallel cc (:vector cc var arg1 arg2 arg ...) (:integers i)))
+     (:parallel cc (:vector var arg1 arg2 arg ...) (:integers i)))
     ((_ cc var arg1 arg2 arg ...)
      (:do cc
           (let ((vec #f)
